  "question": {
    "text": "In which of the following ionization processes, the bond order has increased and the magnetic behaviour has changed?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZffD0",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{C}_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{C}_2^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l8pjd",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{NO} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{NO}^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "k7FqD",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{O}_2^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QWwEB",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{N}_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{N}_2^{+}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In $\\mathrm{C}_2-\\mathrm{C}_2{ }^{+}$electron is removed from bonding molecular orbital so bond order decreases. In $\\mathrm{NO}$ $\\longrightarrow \\mathrm{NO}^{+}$, electron is removed from anti bonding molecular orbital so bond order increases and nature changes from paramagnetic to diamagnetic. \nHence, (B) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
